# What is not sent to the Docker daemon when this image is built.
#
# The Dockerfile copies named paths, so nothing here would reach the image by
# accident today. It is listed anyway: the build context is uploaded whole, a
# `COPY . .` added later would pick up everything in it, and a key that was
# never in the context cannot be committed to a layer by a future edit.
#
# It is also most of the build time. `target/` alone is gigabytes of build
# output that the image rebuilds from source regardless.

# The anchor signing key and the sender's position cache. The key reaches the
# container as a mounted secret at runtime, never through the image.
.anchor/

# Everything demo.sh writes: databases, logs, per-service signing keys.
run/

# Build output, rebuilt inside the image from source.
target/

# Any key or database produced anywhere else.
*.key
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

.git/
.github/
docs/
*.md
